---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro'
import { SITE } from '../lib/config'
---

<BaseLayout title="About — Clinker Brewing Co." description="The story behind Clinker Brewing Co. — brewed on-site at 412 S Main St, Greenville, SC. Owner Marcus Dunlap.">

  <!-- Hero banner -->
  <section class="relative py-28 md:py-36 px-6 overflow-hidden grain">
    <img
      src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1535958636474-b021ee887b13?w=1600&q=80"
      alt="Inside Clinker Brewing taproom"
      class="absolute inset-0 w-full h-full object-cover brightness-[0.15]"
      loading="eager"
    />
    <div class="relative z-10 max-w-3xl mx-auto text-center">
      <h1 class="text-4xl md:text-6xl font-bold text-cream reveal">Our Story</h1>
      <hr class="amber-rule reveal delay-1" />
      <p class="text-warm-light/60 text-lg mt-4 reveal delay-2">
        Not a brand. Not a franchise. A taproom.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Marcus / Origin -->
  <section class="py-20 md:py-28 px-6">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-5xl grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-12 items-center">
      <div class="reveal">
        <p class="text-amber font-heading text-sm uppercase tracking-[0.25em] mb-3">The Founder</p>
        <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-cream">Marcus Dunlap</h2>
        <hr class="amber-rule !mx-0 reveal delay-1" />
        <div class="text-warm-light/70 leading-relaxed space-y-4 mt-4">
          <p>
            Marcus started homebrewing in his garage — not as a business plan, but because he
            couldn't find the beer he wanted to drink. West Coast IPAs with actual bitterness.
            Stouts that tasted like they came from somewhere, not a lab.
          </p>
          <p>
            When the building on South Main opened up — an old railroad warehouse with brick
            walls and stories in every crack — he didn't write a business plan. He moved in the
            kettles, built the bar from reclaimed railroad wood, and started pouring.
          </p>
          <p>
            Clinker Brewing Co. opened its doors with four taps and a prayer. Now there are
            eight, and the prayer's been replaced with a Friday night crowd that doesn't need
            advertising to show up.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="reveal delay-2">
        <div class="rounded-2xl overflow-hidden border border-slag/20 shadow-xl">
          <!-- PHOTO NEEDED: Marcus Dunlap portrait or at brewing equipment -->
          <img
            src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1559526324-593bc073d938?w=800&q=80"
            alt="Marcus Dunlap at the brewing equipment"
            class="w-full aspect-[4/5] object-cover"
            loading="lazy"
          />
        </div>
        <!-- Real portrait photo needed from Marcus -->
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- The Space -->
  <section class="py-20 md:py-28 px-6 bg-coal-lighter">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-5xl">
      <div class="text-center mb-14">
        <h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold text-amber reveal">The Building</h2>
        <hr class="amber-rule reveal delay-1" />
      </div>

      <div class="grid md:grid-cols-3 gap-6 reveal delay-2">
        <div class="rounded-xl overflow-hidden border border-slag/15">
          <img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1532634922-8fe0b757fb13?w=600&q=80" alt="Tap handles and bar" class="aspect-[3/4] object-cover w-full" loading="lazy" />
          <div class="p-4">
            <p class="text-warm-light font-medium text-sm">The Bar</p>
            <p class="text-xs text-slag mt-1">Reclaimed railroad wood. Every scratch earned.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="rounded-xl overflow-hidden border border-slag/15">
          <img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1567696911980-2eed69a46042?w=600&q=80" alt="Brewery exterior" class="aspect-[3/4] object-cover w-full" loading="lazy" />
          <div class="p-4">
            <p class="text-warm-light font-medium text-sm">South Main</p>
            <p class="text-xs text-slag mt-1">412 S Main St — the old railroad warehouse district.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="rounded-xl overflow-hidden border border-slag/15">
          <img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1584225064536-d0fbc0a10f18?w=600&q=80" alt="People in the taproom" class="aspect-[3/4] object-cover w-full" loading="lazy" />
          <div class="p-4">
            <p class="text-warm-light font-medium text-sm">The Crowd</p>
            <p class="text-xs text-slag mt-1">No TVs. No pretense. Just good conversation.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="mt-12 max-w-2xl mx-auto text-center reveal">
        <p class="text-warm-light/70 leading-relaxed">
          The space is industrial because that's what it is — exposed brick, steel beams, concrete floors.
          The vintage rail signage was already on the walls. We just swept the dust off and hung some lights.
          Seats 80 inside, more on the patio when the weather cooperates.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Philosophy -->
  <section class="py-20 md:py-28 px-6">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-4xl">
      <div class="text-center mb-14">
        <h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold text-amber reveal">How We Brew</h2>
        <hr class="amber-rule reveal delay-1" />
      </div>

      <div class="grid sm:grid-cols-3 gap-8 reveal delay-2">
        <div class="text-center">
          <div class="w-14 h-14 rounded-full bg-amber/10 border border-amber/20 flex items-center justify-center mx-auto mb-4">
            <span class="text-2xl">🍺</span>
          </div>
          <h3 class="font-heading text-lg font-semibold text-warm-light uppercase tracking-wide">Brewed On-Site</h3>
          <p class="text-slag text-sm mt-2">
            Every beer is brewed here. No contract brewing, no guest taps pretending to be ours.
            Eight taps, all Clinker.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="text-center">
          <div class="w-14 h-14 rounded-full bg-amber/10 border border-amber/20 flex items-center justify-center mx-auto mb-4">
            <span class="text-2xl">🔄</span>
          </div>
          <h3 class="font-heading text-lg font-semibold text-warm-light uppercase tracking-wide">Always Rotating</h3>
          <p class="text-slag text-sm mt-2">
            The tap list changes every week. When a keg kicks, something new goes on. No permanent
            fixtures — except the Clinker IPA. That one stays.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="text-center">
          <div class="w-14 h-14 rounded-full bg-amber/10 border border-amber/20 flex items-center justify-center mx-auto mb-4">
            <span class="text-2xl">🥃</span>
          </div>
          <h3 class="font-heading text-lg font-semibold text-warm-light uppercase tracking-wide">Barrel-Aged</h3>
          <p class="text-slag text-sm mt-2">
            Limited releases when the barrels are ready. Not on a schedule.
            Midnight Express is our bourbon barrel imperial stout — worth the wait.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Furnace Sessions / Community -->
  <section class="py-20 md:py-28 px-6 bg-coal-lighter">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-4xl grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-12 items-center">
      <div class="reveal">
        <div class="rounded-2xl overflow-hidden border border-slag/15">
          <!-- PHOTO NEEDED: Band performing at Furnace Sessions -->
          <img
            src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1504735217152-b768bcab5ebc?w=800&q=80"
            alt="Live music at the Furnace Sessions"
            class="w-full aspect-video object-cover"
            loading="lazy"
          />
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="reveal delay-2">
        <p class="text-amber font-heading text-sm uppercase tracking-[0.25em] mb-3">Community</p>
        <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-cream">More Than a Taproom</h2>
        <hr class="amber-rule !mx-0" />
        <div class="text-warm-light/70 leading-relaxed space-y-4 mt-4">
          <p>
            <strong class="text-warm-light">The Furnace Sessions</strong> started because Marcus's
            buddy had a band and nowhere to play. Now it's every Friday and Saturday — local bands,
            no cover, the kind of volume that makes conversation optional.
          </p>
          <p>
            <strong class="text-warm-light">Trivia Night</strong> is every Thursday at 7.
            Teams of six, prizes for the top three, and the questions are harder than they should be.
          </p>
          <p>
            We don't have a kitchen — we have food trucks. Rotating schedule Thu–Sun.
            Different truck, same good beer.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Private Events CTA -->
  <section class="py-20 md:py-24 px-6">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-2xl text-center">
      <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-amber reveal">Book the Taproom</h2>
      <hr class="amber-rule reveal delay-1" />
      <p class="text-warm-light/70 text-lg mt-4 reveal delay-1">
        Birthdays, corporate events, rehearsal dinners, release parties.
        80 seated, 120 standing. We'll save you the good stuff.
      </p>
      <a
        href="/contact"
        class="inline-block mt-8 rounded-lg bg-amber px-8 py-3.5 text-base font-semibold text-coal hover:bg-amber-light transition-colors reveal delay-2"
      >
        Get in Touch
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>

</BaseLayout>
